{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c387","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":30,"recorded_at":1780531400000055,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"call_id":"call_01a0ad6e4a77746b93d794c525039673","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-1-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260830-kp4zpu, status=development)' 2>&1; echo \\\"---\\\"; cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-kp4zpu/TASK-260830-kp4zpu_producer.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Set task status and read producer brief\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"primary\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"status_changed\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-kp4zpu\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"development\\\"}}}\\n---\\nOwn TASK-260830-kp4zpu (implement-provider-identity-validation), first leaf of STORY-260830-315721 (provider-identity-profile-and-resume; siblings 3uzfyn profile resolution/persistence and 2zvo8m native resume smoke framework follow you). Implement Provider Identity Record 1.0.0 creation and validation as production code: exact native session IDs, store roots, backend realms, build tuples and discovery evidence per the pinned sections 2.4, 5.5, 7.5-7.7 and 8 (provider/platform matrix), producing records that internal/provhost CheckIdentity/DecodeIdentifyResult and the landed session record/event consumers already accept — extend internal/provhost (or a sibling package it adopts) rather than duplicating its decoders, and drive the landed conformance harness from TASK-260830-32jeti; cover every refusal the sections name (wrong provider id, realm/store-root mismatch, build tuple drift, missing or unsupported discovery evidence, platform rows that are unknown/unsupported per Appendix B gates — never invent parity for a gated cell), with idempotent identity creation and no unsupported capability advertised. Replace the task's v0.5.0 scope citations with the pinned v0.6.0 headings of the same sections. Managed Story worktree contract: the Story worktree is provisioned by task-board under .temp/<STORY-ID>/worktree on branch task-board/story/<STORY-ID> forked from the current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED for the handoff snapshot, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if git fetch origin shows that origin/main moved past the workspace base before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-kp4zpu and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate source, test, harness and documentation paths (no task-board.config.json, no __pycache__/.pyc, no stray plant files; run Python harnesses with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1). Evidence contract: every AC sentence and every gate/refusal is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test or declared a stated bound, reported as a ratio (n of m rows driven, call site named); negatives that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; at least one NARROWING mutant per gate (a token-preserving one where a gate inspects text) executed by a shipped harness on the exact final source with per-plant raw logs, subprocess return-code exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control, and NOT_APPLIED / COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE reported outside the numerator; crash/idempotency evidence with real process termination where the operation mutates durable state; a conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to its owner/test; LOGBOOK.md and internal TRACEABILITY.md updated without unsupported claims; no CLI or unsupported capability advertised. Authority: pinned relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0 commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6 (internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json, embedded internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md) — the section numbers in the task scope refer to the retained headings of that revision; keep historical v0.5.0 (28bf96d) behavior compatible. Reuse the landed shared owners instead of duplicating them: internal/sessrepo (repository, event chain, lease and checkpoint record attestation), internal/sessstate (state reducer), internal/sessquery (selector, plans, winning-lease admission, sealed checkpoint admission), internal/canonicaljson (closed shapes), internal/localstore (paths, projection), internal/provhost (provider identity, manifest, probe, spawn, quiesce), internal/catalog and internal/traceability (contract census; run go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck and the cataloggen -check command from task-board.config.json). Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local, never hosted; run the affected packages while iterating and the full configured validation suite once before the handoff. Budget: the run has 4 hours and the runtime constructs the Change Request with a 26-command suite after your handoff — hand off no later than 3 hours in; if the scope is not finished by then, hand off a coherent partial with the ratio stated honestly rather than exceeding the budget. Attach TASK-260830-kp4zpu_results.md, TASK-260830-kp4zpu_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-kp4zpu_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-kp4zpu --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: codex gpt-5.6-luna max (operator fallback while Muse Spark transport is failing). The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.\\n\",\n  