=E1</code>; resumed carries P1/null |\n674|| <code>PROFILE-TB-TAKEOVER</code> | Task-board start P0 → E1 → export C1 → takeover | Bundle projection carries P1/E1; journaled bridge resume and events use the same pair |\n675|| <code>PROFILE-TB-RESUME</code> | Task-board owner resume from C1 | Bundle, bridge resume, and events agree on P1/E1 |\n676|| <code>PROFILE-TB-FORK</code> | Task-board fork C1 | Source bundle carries P1/E1; new Session Record and bridge resume use P1/null; fork event retains E1 only in <code>source_profile_event_id</code> |\n677|| <code>PROFILE-PI-EQUAL-MAPPING</code> | Pi changes <code>standard</code> to <code>yolo</code> at E1 while both map to <code>default_unrestricted_tool_set</code> | Ax still persists and reports P1/E1; equal provider argv text is not authority to erase E1 |\n678|\n679|Any fixture that uses P0 after C1, omits E1 where the event schema requires its\n680|source, or accepts a bundle profile inconsistent with C1 is\n681|<code>integrity_failure</code> before activation.\n682|\n683|## 3. Architecture and durable local layout\n684|\n685|### 3.1 Required components\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
