{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c757","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":518,"recorded_at":1780531400001031,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6f-62a4-7fc1-b270-5ab59f8e94fe"},"task_id":"01a0ad6f-62a4-7fc1-b270-5ab59f8e94fe","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad6f-62a4-7fc1-b270-5ab59f8e94fe","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3060 line(s) above)\n3061|<code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, and\n3062|<code>rolling_back</code> states and non-null in\n3063|<code>committed|rolled_back</code> states.\n3064|<code>updated_at</code> never precedes <code>created_at</code>, and terminal time\n3065|never precedes either. Timestamps are diagnostics; state, IDs, entry facts, and\n3066|filesystem verification decide recovery.\n3067|\n3068|Every transaction operation receives the same complete\n3069|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>. A fresh plugin process locates state\n3070|only through that authority, validates the path and\n3071|<code>transaction.json</code> IDs before acting, and MUST NOT use an ambient\n3072|transaction registry or search another root. A crash while\n3073|<code>preparing</code>, <code>committing</code>, or <code>rolling_back</code> is\n3074|reconciled from the entries to one exposed status before\n3075|<code>materialize-status</code> responds; an irreconcilable entry is\n3076|<code>integrity_failure</code> and retains the root for diagnosis. Prepared\n3077|documents store the rollback token under owner-only permissions so a later\n3078|process can reconstruct the current durable status; terminal documents set it\n3079|to null.\n3080|Commit removes all backups only after durable committed state; rollback\n3081|restores all predecessors before durable rolled-back state. The terminal\n3082|<code>transaction.json</code> receipt remains until the corresponding\n3083|Materialization Journal is terminal and for at least\n3084|<code>sync.staging_retention_hours</code> afterward. Object-source bytes and\n3085|backup/staged subtrees MAY then be removed; live or ambiguous roots MUST NOT be\n3086|garbage-collected.\n3087|\n3088|In <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code>, <code>unknown</code> requires null\n3089|plan/token/discovery; <code>prepared</code> requires all three non-null;\n3090|<code>committed</code> and <code>rolled_back</code> require a non-null plan and\n3091|discovery proof and a null rollback token. The discovery proof in a rolled-back\n3092|status describes the destination after rollback. An operation failure does not\n3093|invent a status state: it returns the protocol failure envelope, and the next\n3094|status request reports the last durable state. An unreadable or\n3095|integrity-invalid transaction MUST fail with <code>integrity_failure</code> and\n3096|MUST be quarantined rather than represented as a successful status object.\n3097|Every provider mutation request that carries <code>operation_id</code> uses the\n3098|single Provider protocol 2.0.0 idempotency key\n3099|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>. An\n3100|identical canonical mutation request MUST return a byte-identical result across\n3101|a fresh plugin process; any changed member is\n3102|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code> and MUST cause no new mutation. Observational\n3103|operations, including <code>materialize-status</code>, are evolving reads. They\n3104|use the provider envelope's fresh <code>request_id</code> only for correlation,\n3105|MUST NOT be stored as mutation receipts, and MUST return the durable state at\n3106|the read's reconciliation point even when an earlier identical read returned a\n3107|different phase. For <code>capture</code>, replay verifies/reuses only exact\n3108|digest-named files already present in the same Object Sink and re-emits the\n3109|same manifest/descriptors; an extra or changed file fails integrity. Provider\n3110|<code>fork</code> is side-effect-free and recomputes the same plan. The\n3111|materialize mutations use their durable transaction document as the receipt.\n3112|No operation relies on a searched ambient registry. Transaction IDs and\n3113|mutation operation IDs are caller-supplied and stable across retries. For one\n3114|provider materialization transaction, the <code>operation_id</code> is\n3115|transaction-wide across <code>materialize</code> and exactly one terminal\n3116|<code>materialize-commit</code> or <code>materialize-rollback</code>; a\n3117|<code>materialize-status</code> request omits it and locates the transaction only\n3118|through the caller-supplied materialization/transaction IDs and exact authority.\n3119|Reusing the mutation value across distinct operation tags does not alias their\n3120|recorded results. Within one provider ID,\n3121|an operation ID used by the materialize family identifies exactly one materialization transaction:\n3122|its <code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, plan ID, object\n3123|source, transaction authority, provider-store authorities, lease, activation,\n3124|rollback reason, and all remaining body members are immutable retry input for\n3125|their operation tag. Reusing <code>(operation, operation_id)</code> with any\n3126|different canonical body is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>; the plugin MUST\n3127|return the first recorded result or failure and MUST NOT allocate, search, or\n3128|mutate another transaction root. A transaction or materialization ID already\n3129|bound to another operation ID is also <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. There\n3130|is no second tuple- or path-based idempotency key in provider protocol 2.0.0.\n3131|\n3132|The operation body registry is exact. A named schema object means the complete\n3133|validated object, not only its digest. Arrays of schema objects are sorted by\n3134|their canonical identity field and contain no duplicate identity:\n3135|\n3136|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3137|| --- | --- | --- |\n3138|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Provider Manifest object (Section 7.3) |\n3139|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, requested_capabilities:sorted unique capability-name[0..7]}</code> | Provider Probe object (Section 7.4) |\n3140|| <code>launch</code> | <code>{session_record:Session Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, launch_plan:Launch Plan, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\n3141|| <code>identify-session</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7, provider_id:provider-id, observation:ProcessObservation}</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak, matched_evidence:sorted unique native_id&#124;store_path&#124;provider_event&#124;backend_lookup[1..4]}</code> |\n3142|| <code>quiesce</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{proof:SafeBoundaryProof}</code> |\n3143|| <code>native-store-plan</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanRequest</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_host_id:UUIDv7, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_manifest_id:digest, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanResult</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, materialization_plan:Materialization Plan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], path_key_rewrites:map(UUIDv7,string[1..1024])[0..256]}</code> |\n3144|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, proof:SafeBoundaryProof, object_sink:ObjectSink, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, capture_id:UUIDv7, manifest:Transfer Manifest, blob_descriptors:sorted unique Blob Descriptor[0..32768], written_blob_ids:sorted unique digest[0..32768], captured_store_generation:string[1..512], exclusions_applied:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code> |\n3145|| <code>materialize</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan:Materialization Plan, object_source:ProviderObjectSourceAuthority, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:prepared, created_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], merged_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], validations:ValidationEvidence[1..256], rollback_token:base64url-256+, native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof}</code> |\n3146|| <code>materialize-status</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority}</code> | <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> |\n3147|| <code>materialize-commit</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, rollback_token:base64url-256+, activation:dormant_validated&#124;owner_resumed, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:committed, backup_removed:boolean, committed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n3148|| <code>materialize-rollback</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, rollback_token:base64url-256+, reason:lease_lost&#124;validation_failed&#124;resume_failed&#124;operator_abort&#124;crash_recovery}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:rolled_back, restored_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], removed_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], native_discovery_absent:boolean}</code> |\n3149|| <code>resume</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\n3150|| <code>fork</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, source_identity:Provider Identity Record, source_checkpoint:Checkpoint Record, new_session_record:Session Record, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, result_kind:native_fork&#124;supported_import, planned_native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null, spawn_plan:SpawnPlan, requires_provider_materialization:boolean, provenance_verified:boolean}</code> |\n3151|| <code>stop</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, mode:graceful&#124;force, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{closure:ProcessClosure}</code> |\n3152|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, identity:Provider Identity Record&#124;null}</code> | <code>{provider_id:provider-id, provider_version:string[1..128]&#124;null, findings:DoctorFinding[0..1024]}</code> |\n3153|\n3154|For <code>launch</code>, the profile and launch plan MUST exactly equal their\n3155|Session Record values. Provider <code>fork</code> is a planning call: it MUST\n3156|NOT write a provider store, allocate an active backend conversation, or start a\n3157|process. Its operation ID is the Session Record's\n3158|<code>fork_provenance.operation_id</code>; an identical retry returns the same\n3159|plan and any changed body is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. The new record\n3160|MUST contain Fork Provenance matching the source/checkpoint and operation, and\n3161|a successful result requires <code>provenance_verified = true</code> and MUST\n3162|NOT describe a blank session. <code>native_fork</code> requires\n3163|<code>requires_provider_materialization = false</code> and MAY have a planned\n3164|native ID when the provider allocates it only at process start.\n3165|<code>supported_import</code> requires\n3166|<code>requires_provider_materialization = true</code>; the coordinator then\n3167|calls <code>native-store-plan phase=materialize</code> with\n3168|<code>mode=fork</code> and includes the validated provider plan in the\n3169|destination materialization transaction. In both variants, a new Provider\n3170|Identity Record is authoritative only after native discovery following the\n3171|prepared transaction; the planned ID is an expectation, not an identity\n3172|record.\n3173|\n3174|<code>launch</code>, <code>resume</code>, and <code>fork</code> return plans; the\n3175|trusted terminal backend performs process creation. Plugins MUST NOT return\n3176|secret environment values. <code>native-store-plan</code> succeeds only for an\n3177|advertised portable-store tuple and MUST separate durable includes,\n3178|machine-local excludes, path-key rewrites, quiescence preconditions, and\n3179|validation steps. Its two request and result variants are closed and disjoint:\n3180|a capture request has no destination platform, destination host, destination\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
