{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c781","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":539,"recorded_at":1780531400001073,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6f-6cb1-7ed3-a10c-e5ed361942e9"},"task_id":"01a0ad6f-6cb1-7ed3-a10c-e5ed361942e9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad6f-6cb1-7ed3-a10c-e5ed361942e9","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3179 line(s) above)\n3180|a capture request has no destination platform, destination host, destination\n3181|workspace map, or source manifest; a materialize request has no source\n3182|workspace map. Capture therefore works for the first local checkpoint without\n3183|inventing a destination peer or a source-as-destination sentinel.\n3184|\n3185|The capture result's authorities are the complete provider source-root\n3186|authority for that capture. A materialize plan MUST contain at least one\n3187|Section 10.5 <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority with\n3188|<code>prepared_for_host_id = destination_host_id</code>. Every such authority\n3189|MUST have the same provider/platform as the request, resolve to a\n3190|destination-local native-store root for the exact adapter tuple, and be\n3191|disjoint from ax data/state/cache/runtime roots, task-board staging,\n3192|workspaces, and credential/authentication roots unless an exact child path is\n3193|the provider's documented durable store. A path-key rewrite is keyed by logical\n3194|workspace ID and contains destination-derived non-secret cache-key data, never\n3195|a source absolute path. An unavailable surface returns the common failure\n3196|envelope, not a success body with a null required plan.\n3197|\n3198|The following source-only first-checkpoint body and result are the normative\n3199|<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-POS</code> fixture. Their absence of every\n3200|destination member is intentional:\n3201|\n3202|~~~json\n3203|{\n3204|  \"phase\": \"capture\",\n3205|  \"identity\": {\n3206|    \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3207|    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3208|    \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3209|    \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3210|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3211|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3212|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3213|    \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3214|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3215|    \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3216|    \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3217|    \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3218|    \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3219|    \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3220|    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3221|    \"extensions\": {}\n3222|  },\n3223|  \"source_platform\": \"macos\",\n3224|  \"mode\": \"snapshot\",\n3225|  \"source_workspace_paths\": {\n3226|    \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/payments-api\"\n3227|  },\n3228|  \"lease\": {\n3229|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3230|    \"lease_epoch\": 1,\n3231|    \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3232|  }\n3233|}\n3234|~~~\n3235|\n3236|~~~json\n3237|{\n3238|  \"phase\": \"capture\",\n3239|  \"capture_plan\": {\n3240|    \"capture_id\": \"0198f4c8-0790-72aa-8374-3234567890ab\",\n3241|    \"source_authorities\": [\n3242|      {\n3243|        \"authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n3244|        \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3245|        \"platform\": \"macos\",\n3246|        \"root_path\": \"/Users/iv/.codex/sessions\",\n3247|        \"root_role\": \"durable_store\",\n3248|        \"access\": \"capture_source\"\n3249|      }\n3250|    ],\n3251|    \"items\": [\n3252|      {\n3253|        \"source_authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n3254|        \"source_relative_path\": \"2026/08/19/rollout-11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555.jsonl\",\n3255|        \"manifest_path\": \"session/rollout.jsonl\",\n3256|        \"kind\": \"file\",\n3257|        \"state_class\": \"durable_payload\",\n3258|        \"required\": true\n3259|      }\n3260|    ],\n3261|    \"excluded_targets\": [],\n3262|    \"store_generation\": \"closed:11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555:1\",\n3263|    \"snapshot_requires_closed_store\": true\n3264|  },\n3265|  \"include_classes\": [\"durable_payload\"],\n3266|  \"exclude_classes\": [\"credential\",\"live_pid\",\"machine_auth\",\"socket\",\"transient_lock\"]\n3267|}\n3268|~~~\n3269|\n3270|<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N1</code> adds\n3271|<code>destination_platform</code> to the capture body and MUST fail with\n3272|<code>incompatible_schema</code>. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N2</code> changes\n3273|the item authority to an undeclared ID and MUST fail before any provider byte\n3274|is read. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N3</code> makes the source authority equal\n3275|the credential root and MUST fail with <code>secret_policy_violation</code>.\n3276|\n3277|<code>capture</code> is the only provider operation that may emit provider\n3278|payload bytes. It requires <code>proof.safe = true</code>, equal proof/plan store\n3279|generation, and the current lease. Its manifest MUST have\n3280|<code>kind = provider</code>, the session as subject, and exactly the returned\n3281|descriptor/blob closure. The host MUST reject an extra sink file, missing\n3282|required item, descriptor mismatch, excluded class/path, generation change, or\n3283|secret-policy violation and MUST discard the isolated sink without importing\n3284|it. The plugin MUST NOT write a live ax store, live SQLite index, credential\n3285|root, or destination native store during capture.\n3286|\n3287|Provider materialization is a recoverable two-decision transaction.\n3288|<code>materialize</code> applies the exact plan while retaining every replaced\n3289|destination byte under the authorized transaction layout and returns\n3290|<code>state = prepared</code>; it MUST NOT delete its backup. While prepared,\n3291|the host validates exact native discovery and either keeps the replica dormant\n3292|or starts the winning owner. It then calls <code>materialize-commit</code> to\n3293|discard the backup, or <code>materialize-rollback</code> to restore it. Commit\n3294|requires <code>backup_removed = true</code>; rollback requires the native\n3295|identity introduced by the transaction to be absent afterward unless it was a\n3296|pre-existing backend identity. A rollback token is machine-local recovery\n3297|authority, MUST be at least 256 random bits, MUST be stored only in the\n3298|owner-only Materialization Journal and prepared Provider Transaction Document,\n3299|and MUST NOT be replicated or logged.\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
