{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7ab","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":560,"recorded_at":1780531400001115,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6f-776c-78d2-b1cf-f2cc06e0efb3"},"task_id":"01a0ad6f-776c-78d2-b1cf-f2cc06e0efb3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad6f-776c-78d2-b1cf-f2cc06e0efb3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3298 line(s) above)\n3299|and MUST NOT be replicated or logged.\n3300|\n3301|The provider plugin MUST execute only plan operations whose authority has\n3302|<code>kind = provider_store</code> and whose <code>provider_id</code> equals the\n3303|plugin manifest ID. The ax host executes workspace and task-board operations;\n3304|it MUST reject a plugin response that reports any created or merged path\n3305|outside the selected provider-store authorities. The plugin resolves each\n3306|reported absolute path from that authority's root plus the operation's\n3307|relative target, rechecks the predecessor immediately before mutation, and\n3308|uses no unlisted native-store root. A composite plan is therefore one host\n3309|transaction containing disjoint authority-specific executors, not a grant for\n3310|the provider plugin to mutate the workspace.\n3311|\n3312|The three mutation operations use the same parent <code>operation_id</code>,\n3313|<code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, and byte-identical\n3314|transaction authority. The sole mutation idempotency key remains\n3315|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>; the materialization and transaction IDs\n3316|are immutable non-key inputs. Each mutation tag therefore has a distinct key\n3317|while all phases locate the same authority. A retry of one mutation name MUST\n3318|use byte-identical canonical arguments. <code>materialize-status</code> omits\n3319|<code>operation_id</code>; it is the required evolving lost-response recovery\n3320|read and uses the envelope <code>request_id</code> only for correlation. A status\n3321|read MUST reconcile and return the current durable state, so a read that once\n3322|returned <code>prepared</code> may later return <code>committed</code> or\n3323|<code>rolled_back</code>. An unknown transaction MUST return state\n3324|<code>unknown</code>; the host MUST NOT infer success. A prepared transaction\n3325|survives plugin/host restart until explicit commit or rollback. A plugin that\n3326|cannot provide this prepare/status/commit/rollback behavior MUST advertise\n3327|<code>portable_store</code> disabled.\n3328|\n3329|Normative prepared result body:\n3330|\n3331|~~~json\n3332|{\n3333|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3334|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n3335|  \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n3336|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n3337|  \"state\": \"prepared\",\n3338|  \"created_paths\": [\"/srv/provider/sessions/11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"],\n3339|  \"merged_paths\": [],\n3340|  \"validations\": [\n3341|    {\"code\":\"native_discovery\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"detail\":\"exact session identity resolved\"}\n3342|  ],\n3343|  \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n3344|  \"native_discovery\": {\n3345|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3346|    \"discovered\": true,\n3347|    \"discovery_root\": \"/srv/provider/sessions\",\n3348|    \"backend_resolved\": false\n3349|  }\n3350|}\n3351|~~~\n3352|\n3353|The normative transaction cases are:\n3354|\n3355|| Fixture | Calls | Required terminal state |\n3356|| --- | --- | --- |\n3357|| <code>PTX-POS-DORMANT</code> | materialize → status prepared → commit with <code>dormant_validated</code> | committed; replica remains unable to run |\n3358|| <code>PTX-POS-OWNER</code> | materialize → exact discovery → owner resume → commit with <code>owner_resumed</code> | committed; backup removed only after resume evidence |\n3359|| <code>PTX-ROLLBACK</code> | materialize → validation failure → rollback | predecessor bytes restored; introduced identity absent |\n3360|| <code>PTX-LOST-PREPARE</code> | materialize response lost → status prepared | same token/plan returned; no second destination mutation |\n3361|| <code>PTX-LOST-COMMIT</code> | commit response lost → status committed | caller records commit; MUST NOT roll back |\n3362|| <code>PTX-STATUS-EVOLVES</code> | status returns prepared → commit succeeds → the same status body is read under a fresh envelope request ID | second read returns committed; no byte-identical replay rule applies to either observation |\n3363|| <code>PTX-UNKNOWN</code> | status unknown after an ambiguous call | fail closed and quarantine transaction root; MUST NOT infer prepare or commit |\n3364|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-COMMIT</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 status reads the same authority/document → P3 commits and exits → P4 status reads the terminal receipt | prepared and committed facts, token, plan, and discovery are identical across processes; backup bytes are removed only by P3 |\n3365|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-ROLLBACK</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 rolls back with the same authority/token → P3 status reads the terminal receipt | every predecessor is restored, every introduced target is absent, and no process searches outside the passed authority |\n3366|\n3367|Changing a plan, object-source authority, or transaction authority on a repeated\n3368|<code>materialize</code>, changing activation/lease on a repeated commit, or\n3369|changing rollback reason/token on a repeated rollback while reusing the same\n3370|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code> key is the normative negative\n3371|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-N1</code> fixture and returns\n3372|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3373|\n3374|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N1</code> loses a prepared response and retries the\n3375|same <code>(materialize, operation_id)</code> while changing only\n3376|<code>materialization_id</code>; <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N2</code> changes only\n3377|<code>transaction_id</code>; and <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N3</code> changes only\n3378|one authority root. Each MUST return <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, leave the\n3379|original transaction document/root byte-identical, and create no second root.\n3380|\n3381|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-LEASE</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-VALIDATION</code>,\n3382|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-RESUME</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-OPERATOR</code>, and\n3383|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-CRASH</code> repeat the rollback path with, respectively,\n3384|<code>lease_lost</code>, <code>validation_failed</code>,\n3385|<code>resume_failed</code>, <code>operator_abort</code>, and\n3386|<code>crash_recovery</code>. Each reason is persisted before restoration and\n3387|replaying the same request returns the same terminal result; changing only the\n3388|reason is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3389|\n3390|Normative <code>resume</code> request body and success body:\n3391|\n3392|~~~json\n3393|{\n3394|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3395|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3396|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3397|  \"operation\": \"resume\",\n3398|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:20:00.000Z\",\n3399|  \"body\": {\n3400|    \"identity\": {\n3401|      \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3402|      \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3403|      \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3404|      \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3405|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3406|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3407|      \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3408|      \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3409|      \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3410|      \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3411|      \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3412|      \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3413|      \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3414|      \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3415|      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3416|      \"extensions\": {}\n3417|    },\n3418|    \"workspace_paths\": {\n3419|      \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api\"\n3420|    },\n3421|    \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n3422|    \"terminal\": {\n3423|      \"backend\": \"tmux\",\n3424|      \"terminal_id\": \"ax-payments-api\",\n3425|      \"interactive\": true,\n3426|      \"columns\": 120,\n3427|      \"rows\": 40\n3428|    },\n3429|    \"lease\": {\n3430|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3431|      \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n3432|      \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3433|    }\n3434|  }\n3435|}\n3436|~~~\n3437|\n3438|~~~json\n3439|{\n3440|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3441|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3442|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3443|  \"ok\": true,\n3444|  \"body\": {\n3445|    \"argv\": [\n3446|      \"codex\",\n3447|      \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3448|      \"resume\",\n3449|      \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"\n3450|    ],\n3451|    \"cwd\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api/src\",\n3452|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n3453|    \"env_literals\": {},\n3454|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3455|    \"profile_mapping\": \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3456|    \"extensions\": {}\n3457|  }\n3458|}\n3459|~~~\n3460|\n3461|### 7.6 Quiescence proof\n3462|\n3463|A successful <code>quiesce</code> response MUST contain:\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7ad","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":561,"recorded_at":1780531400001117,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6f-776c-78d2-b1cf-f2cc06e0efb3"},"task_id":"01a0ad6f-776c-78d2-b1cf-f2cc06e0efb3","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ad6f-776c-78d2-b1cf-f2cc06e0efb3"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7af","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":562,"recorded_at":1780531400001119,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"call_id":"call_01a0ad6f72f472bdafe2351949728a8d","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3298 line(s) above)\n3299|and MUST NOT be replicated or logged.\n3300|\n3301|The provider plugin MUST execute only plan operations whose authority has\n3302|<code>kind = provider_store</code> and whose <code>provider_id</code> equals the\n3303|plugin manifest ID. The ax host executes workspace and task-board operations;\n3304|it MUST reject a plugin response that reports any created or merged path\n3305|outside the selected provider-store authorities. The plugin resolves each\n3306|reported absolute path from that authority's root plus the operation's\n3307|relative target, rechecks the predecessor immediately before mutation, and\n3308|uses no unlisted native-store root. A composite plan is therefore one host\n3309|transaction containing disjoint authority-specific executors, not a grant for\n3310|the provider plugin to mutate the workspace.\n3311|\n3312|The three mutation operations use the same parent <code>operation_id</code>,\n3313|<code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, and byte-identical\n3314|transaction authority. The sole mutation idempotency key remains\n3315|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>; the materialization and transaction IDs\n3316|are immutable non-key inputs. Each mutation tag therefore has a distinct key\n3317|while all phases locate the same authority. A retry of one mutation name MUST\n3318|use byte-identical canonical arguments. <code>materialize-status</code> omits\n3319|<code>operation_id</code>; it is the required evolving lost-response recovery\n3320|read and uses the envelope <code>request_id</code> only for correlation. A status\n3321|read MUST reconcile and return the current durable state, so a read that once\n3322|returned <code>prepared</code> may later return <code>committed</code> or\n3323|<code>rolled_back</code>. An unknown transaction MUST return state\n3324|<code>unknown</code>; the host MUST NOT infer success. A prepared transaction\n3325|survives plugin/host restart until explicit commit or rollback. A plugin that\n3326|cannot provide this prepare/status/commit/rollback behavior MUST advertise\n3327|<code>portable_store</code> disabled.\n3328|\n3329|Normative prepared result body:\n3330|\n3331|~~~json\n3332|{\n3333|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3334|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n3335|  \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n3336|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n3337|  \"state\": \"prepared\",\n3338|  \"created_paths\": [\"/srv/provider/sessions/11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"],\n3339|  \"merged_paths\": [],\n3340|  \"validations\": [\n3341|    {\"code\":\"native_discovery\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"detail\":\"exact session identity resolved\"}\n3342|  ],\n3343|  \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n3344|  \"native_discovery\": {\n3345|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3346|    \"discovered\": true,\n3347|    \"discovery_root\": \"/srv/provider/sessions\",\n3348|    \"backend_resolved\": false\n3349|  }\n3350|}\n3351|~~~\n3352|\n3353|The normative transaction cases are:\n3354|\n3355|| Fixture | Calls | Required terminal state |\n3356|| --- | --- | --- |\n3357|| <code>PTX-POS-DORMANT</code> | materialize → status prepared → commit with <code>dormant_validated</code> | committed; replica remains unable to run |\n3358|| <code>PTX-POS-OWNER</code> | materialize → exact discovery → owner resume → commit with <code>owner_resumed</code> | committed; backup removed only after resume evidence |\n3359|| <code>PTX-ROLLBACK</code> | materialize → validation failure → rollback | predecessor bytes restored; introduced identity absent |\n3360|| <code>PTX-LOST-PREPARE</code> | materialize response lost → status prepared | same token/plan returned; no second destination mutation |\n3361|| <code>PTX-LOST-COMMIT</code> | commit response lost → status committed | caller records commit; MUST NOT roll back |\n3362|| <code>PTX-STATUS-EVOLVES</code> | status returns prepared → commit succeeds → the same status body is read under a fresh envelope request ID | second read returns committed; no byte-identical replay rule applies to either observation |\n3363|| <code>PTX-UNKNOWN</code> | status unknown after an ambiguous call | fail closed and quarantine transaction root; MUST NOT infer prepare or commit |\n3364|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-COMMIT</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 status reads the same authority/document → P3 commits and exits → P4 status reads the terminal receipt | prepared and committed facts, token, plan, and discovery are identical across processes; backup bytes are removed only by P3 |\n3365|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-ROLLBACK</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 rolls back with the same authority/token → P3 status reads the terminal receipt | every predecessor is restored, every introduced target is absent, and no process searches outside the passed authority |\n3366|\n3367|Changing a plan, object-source authority, or transaction authority on a repeated\n3368|<code>materialize</code>, changing activation/lease on a repeated commit, or\n3369|changing rollback reason/token on a repeated rollback while reusing the same\n3370|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code> key is the normative negative\n3371|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-N1</code> fixture and returns\n3372|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3373|\n3374|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N1</code> loses a prepared response and retries the\n3375|same <code>(materialize, operation_id)</code> while changing only\n3376|<code>materialization_id</code>; <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N2</code> changes only\n3377|<code>transaction_id</code>; and <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N3</code> changes only\n3378|one authority root. Each MUST return <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, leave the\n3379|original transaction document/root byte-identical, and create no second root.\n3380|\n3381|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-LEASE</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-VALIDATION</code>,\n3382|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-RESUME</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-OPERATOR</code>, and\n3383|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-CRASH</code> repeat the rollback path with, respectively,\n3384|<code>lease_lost</code>, <code>validation_failed</code>,\n3385|<code>resume_failed</code>, <code>operator_abort</code>, and\n3386|<code>crash_recovery</code>. Each reason is persisted before restoration and\n3387|replaying the same request returns the same terminal result; changing only the\n3388|reason is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3389|\n3390|Normative <code>resume</code> request body and success body:\n3391|\n3392|~~~json\n3393|{\n3394|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3395|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3396|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3397|  \"operation\": \"resume\",\n3398|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:20:00.000Z\",\n3399|  \"body\": {\n3400|    \"identity\": {\n3401|      \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3402|      \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3403|      \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3404|      \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3405|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3406|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3407|      \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3408|      \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3409|      \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3410|      \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3411|      \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3412|      \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3413|      \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3414|      \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3415|      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3416|      \"extensions\": {}\n3417|    },\n3418|    \"workspace_paths\": {\n3419|      \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api\"\n3420|    },\n3421|    \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n3422|    \"terminal\": {\n3423|      \"backend\": \"tmux\",\n3424|      \"terminal_id\": \"ax-payments-api\",\n3425|      \"interactive\": true,\n3426|      \"columns\": 120,\n3427|      \"rows\": 40\n3428|    },\n3429|    \"lease\": {\n3430|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3431|      \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n3432|      \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3433|    }\n3434|  }\n3435|}\n3436|~~~\n3437|\n3438|~~~json\n3439|{\n3440|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3441|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3442|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3443|  \"ok\": true,\n3444|  \"body\": {\n3445|    \"argv\": [\n3446|      \"codex\",\n3447|      \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3448|      \"resume\",\n3449|      \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"\n3450|    ],\n3451|    \"cwd\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api/src\",\n3452|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n3453|    \"env_literals\": {},\n3454|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3455|    \"profile_mapping\": \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3456|    \"extensions\": {}\n3457|  }\n3458|}\n3459|~~~\n3460|\n3461|### 7.6 Quiescence proof\n3462|\n3463|A successful <code>quiesce</code> response MUST contain:\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
