{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7db","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":584,"recorded_at":1780531400001163,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6f-7fc2-7b50-8d3e-005ef1044327"},"task_id":"01a0ad6f-7fc2-7b50-8d3e-005ef1044327","event":{"kind":"started","task_id":"01a0ad6f-7fc2-7b50-8d3e-005ef1044327","span_id":"47003618dd82cc2d"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7dd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":585,"recorded_at":1780531400001165,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6f-7fc2-7b50-8d3e-005ef1044327"},"task_id":"01a0ad6f-7fc2-7b50-8d3e-005ef1044327","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad6f-7fc2-7b50-8d3e-005ef1044327","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3460 line(s) above)\n3461|### 7.6 Quiescence proof\n3462|\n3463|A successful <code>quiesce</code> response MUST contain:\n3464|\n3465|- provider ID and exact version;\n3466|- <code>input_blocked = true</code>;\n3467|- a provider-specific terminal/idle event reference;\n3468|- <code>foreground_idle = true</code>;\n3469|- <code>background_idle = true</code> when the provider can prove it;\n3470|- open child process and open durable-database handle counts, both zero;\n3471|- the last stable provider-store digest or metadata generation; and\n3472|- <code>safe = true</code>.\n3473|\n3474|If background idleness, process exit, or store closure cannot be proven,\n3475|<code>safe</code> MUST be false and graceful takeover MUST stop. A force\n3476|takeover is a separate operator action; the plugin MUST NOT silently convert the\n3477|request.\n3478|\n3479|For a safe direct-provider proof, Checkpoint Safe Boundary Evidence copies\n3480|provider ID/version, input/idle booleans, and maps\n3481|<code>open_child_count</code> to <code>open_processes</code> and\n3482|<code>open_database_handle_count</code> to\n3483|<code>open_database_handles</code>; <code>evidence</code> is the accepted\n3484|adapter mechanism (<code>provider_api</code>, <code>provider_event</code>,\n3485|<code>managed_pty</code>, or <code>accepted_test</code>). RPC\n3486|<code>SafeBoundary</code> additionally copies the boundary reference and store\n3487|generation, sets <code>store_stable = true</code>, and normalizes\n3488|<code>child_process_open</code> to <code>process_open</code>. No other lossy or\n3489|provider-defined mapping is permitted.\n3490|\n3491|### 7.7 Profile mapping\n3492|\n3493|The v0.3.0 <code>yolo</code> mappings are:\n3494|\n3495|| Provider | Required adapter mapping |\n3496|| --- | --- |\n3497|| Codex | <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> (alias <code>--yolo</code> is accepted by current CLI but the long form SHOULD be persisted in diagnostics) |\n3498|| Claude | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3499|| Gemini CLI | <code>--approval-mode=yolo</code> |\n3500|| Muse | <code>--yolo</code> |\n3501|| Antigravity | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3502|| Pi 0.73.1 | No invented flag; use the provider's default full built-in tool set and report <code>profile_mapping = \"default_unrestricted_tool_set\"</code> |\n3503|\n3504|<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior\n3505|and MUST omit every unrestricted flag above. It MUST NOT reuse a machine-local\n3506|alias that silently expands to unrestricted mode. Provider-specific standard\n3507|options in a sanitized launch plan are applied only after an exact-version\n3508|probe accepts them.\n3509|\n3510|For Pi 0.73.1, both profiles resolve to the provider's same default full tool\n3511|set because no provider permission-mode flag exists. Probe and launch output\n3512|MUST disclose that equivalence; <code>ax</code> ownership, mesh, conflict, and\n3513|confirmation controls still apply.\n3514|\n3515|The adapter MUST probe the exact provider version before applying a mapping.\n3516|An absent or changed flag fails closed.\n3517|\n3518|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3519|\n3520|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3521|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3522|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3523|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3524|\n3525|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3526|| --- | --- |\n3527|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3528|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3529|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3530|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3531|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3532|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3533|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3534|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3535|\n3536|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3537|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3538|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3539|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3540|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3541|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3542|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3543|\n3544|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3545|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3546|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3547|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3548|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3549|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3550|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3551|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3552|\n3553|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3554|\n3555|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7df","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":586,"recorded_at":1780531400001167,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6f-7fc2-7b50-8d3e-005ef1044327"},"task_id":"01a0ad6f-7fc2-7b50-8d3e-005ef1044327","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ad6f-7fc2-7b50-8d3e-005ef1044327"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7e1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":587,"recorded_at":1780531400001169,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"call_id":"call_01a0ad6f7bec74d48fad6fe5461c79d3","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3460 line(s) above)\n3461|### 7.6 Quiescence proof\n3462|\n3463|A successful <code>quiesce</code> response MUST contain:\n3464|\n3465|- provider ID and exact version;\n3466|- <code>input_blocked = true</code>;\n3467|- a provider-specific terminal/idle event reference;\n3468|- <code>foreground_idle = true</code>;\n3469|- <code>background_idle = true</code> when the provider can prove it;\n3470|- open child process and open durable-database handle counts, both zero;\n3471|- the last stable provider-store digest or metadata generation; and\n3472|- <code>safe = true</code>.\n3473|\n3474|If background idleness, process exit, or store closure cannot be proven,\n3475|<code>safe</code> MUST be false and graceful takeover MUST stop. A force\n3476|takeover is a separate operator action; the plugin MUST NOT silently convert the\n3477|request.\n3478|\n3479|For a safe direct-provider proof, Checkpoint Safe Boundary Evidence copies\n3480|provider ID/version, input/idle booleans, and maps\n3481|<code>open_child_count</code> to <code>open_processes</code> and\n3482|<code>open_database_handle_count</code> to\n3483|<code>open_database_handles</code>; <code>evidence</code> is the accepted\n3484|adapter mechanism (<code>provider_api</code>, <code>provider_event</code>,\n3485|<code>managed_pty</code>, or <code>accepted_test</code>). RPC\n3486|<code>SafeBoundary</code> additionally copies the boundary reference and store\n3487|generation, sets <code>store_stable = true</code>, and normalizes\n3488|<code>child_process_open</code> to <code>process_open</code>. No other lossy or\n3489|provider-defined mapping is permitted.\n3490|\n3491|### 7.7 Profile mapping\n3492|\n3493|The v0.3.0 <code>yolo</code> mappings are:\n3494|\n3495|| Provider | Required adapter mapping |\n3496|| --- | --- |\n3497|| Codex | <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> (alias <code>--yolo</code> is accepted by current CLI but the long form SHOULD be persisted in diagnostics) |\n3498|| Claude | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3499|| Gemini CLI | <code>--approval-mode=yolo</code> |\n3500|| Muse | <code>--yolo</code> |\n3501|| Antigravity | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3502|| Pi 0.73.1 | No invented flag; use the provider's default full built-in tool set and report <code>profile_mapping = \"default_unrestricted_tool_set\"</code> |\n3503|\n3504|<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior\n3505|and MUST omit every unrestricted flag above. It MUST NOT reuse a machine-local\n3506|alias that silently expands to unrestricted mode. Provider-specific standard\n3507|options in a sanitized launch plan are applied only after an exact-version\n3508|probe accepts them.\n3509|\n3510|For Pi 0.73.1, both profiles resolve to the provider's same default full tool\n3511|set because no provider permission-mode flag exists. Probe and launch output\n3512|MUST disclose that equivalence; <code>ax</code> ownership, mesh, conflict, and\n3513|confirmation controls still apply.\n3514|\n3515|The adapter MUST probe the exact provider version before applying a mapping.\n3516|An absent or changed flag fails closed.\n3517|\n3518|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3519|\n3520|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3521|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3522|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3523|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3524|\n3525|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3526|| --- | --- |\n3527|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3528|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3529|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3530|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3531|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3532|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3533|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3534|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3535|\n3536|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3537|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3538|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3539|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3540|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3541|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3542|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3543|\n3544|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3545|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3546|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3547|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3548|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3549|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3550|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3551|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3552|\n3553|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3554|\n3555|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
