ses.\\\"\\n },\\n {\\n  \\\"key\\\": \\\"section:18.4\\\",\\n  \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 18.4 requires audit retention - the exact Section 5.2 event types for lease change, force confirmation, managed replacement, task-board launch and adoption and tombstone issuance and resolution, and retention of the event and every referenced immutable object for as long as the Session Record. No retention, expiry or garbage-collection rule is implemented.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"internal/localstore/projection.go opens, rebuilds and recovers the SQLite projection and installs immutable blobs; it declares no retention, expiry or garbage-collection behaviour, and the binding this entry replaces named OpenProjection with the same two storage acceptance cases already used by the Section 3.3 binding.\\\"\\n },\\n {\\n  \\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.1\\\",\\n  \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.1 requires SSH host-channel launch with exclusive TLS 1.3, ALPN ax-host/1 and full mutual certificate authentication; no launcher, TLS endpoint or handshake exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-z1yxg9.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The repository carries no TLS, X.509 or SSH-launch code: provhost speaks the provider-plugin protocol over stdio, secprim checks argv, environment and paths, and the mesh RPC layer is catalog vocabulary without a transport.\\\"\\n },\\n {\\n  \\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.2\\\",\\n  \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.2 requires certificate issuance into a machine-local trust store with enrolled roots and exact leaf checks; no issuance, store or enrollment implementation exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260909-2ez769.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"No certificate, key custody or trust-store code exists: internal/config reads TOML only, internal/localstore keeps blobs and a SQLite projection, and the two new pin fixtures are byte identities without a Go consumer.\\\"\\n },\\n {\\n  \\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.3\\\",\\n  \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.3 requires credential rotation, revocation and authorization generations that refuse stale trust; no rotation or revocation implementation exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260909-2ez769.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Nothing in the tree rotates or revokes credentials: there is no credential store to rotate, no revocation list reader, and no authorization-generation check outside the specification text.\\\"\\n },\\n {\\n  \\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.4\\\",\\n  \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.4 bounds host-channel assurance and e\\n\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3011,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 753,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
