very matrix\\n9967:### 13.13 Crash/restart outcome gate\\n10041:### 13.14 Cross-environment clone\\n10985:### 13.15 Directory continuation planning and execution\\n11120:## 14. CLI and operator experience\\n11122:### 14.1 Command surface\\n11377:### 14.2 Common flags and output\\n11515:### 14.3 Normative examples\\n11643:### 14.4 List and status fields\\n11662:### 14.5 Session Directory CLI Result 3, query, and TUI\\n11807:### 14.6 CLI Result 4.0.0 TerminalBackend surfaces\\n11868:### 14.7 Session selector 1.0.0 and CLI Result 5.0.0\\n14701:## 15. Errors and exit semantics\\n14703:### 15.1 Structured Error\\n14812:### 15.2 Exit codes\\n14835:### 15.3 Stable error codes\\n14953:## 16. Security and threat boundary\\n14955:### 16.1 Trusted mesh model\\n14976:### 16.2 Mandatory exclusions\\n15016:### 16.3 Path and filesystem safety\\n15035:### 16.4 Command and plugin safety\\n15065:### 16.5 Force-takeover risk\\n15077:### 16.6 Out of scope\\n15087:### 16.7 Directory, enrichment, query, and terminal safety\\n15134:## 17. Compatibility and migration\\n15136:### 17.1 Semantic-version rules\\n15188:### 17.2 Reader/writer behavior\\n15206:### 17.3 Immutable data migration\\n15223:### 17.4 Upgrade and downgrade\\n15246:### 17.5 Directory release compatibility\\n15297:## 18. Observability and operations\\n15299:### 18.1 Observation Event\\n15400:### 18.2 Required events\\n15457:### 18.3 Metrics and health\\n15518:### 18.4 Audit retention\\n15543:## 19. <code>ax</code> implementation conformance and product release\\n15545:### 19.1 Implementation phases\\n===\\n109:Other provider references are listed in Appendix C. When provider documentation\\n15739:| <code>AC-WIRE-001</code> | Every Section 1.5 contract and every embedded tagged variant in Appendix D accepts its positive fixture and rejects missing, null-invalid, enum-invalid, unsafe-number, oversized, forbidden-variant, and unknown members. Schema/path-directed common-type vectors reject non-prefixed invalid digests, malformed UUIDv4/UUIDv7, impossible calendar timestamps, and unsorted/duplicate nested arrays even after self-ID recomputation. |\\n15904:## Appendix A. Normative traceability\\n15912:| Providers and native stores | Sections 7, 8, 13.1, 13.6–13.13, Appendix C |\\n15928:| All settled decisions are traceable | Appendix A.1 |\\n15949:| No unresolved implementation question except provider version gates | Appendix B |\\n15950:| Crash/restart classification has one exhaustive outcome and preserves owner/native identity | Sections 13.13, 19.4 <code>AC-CRASH-001</code>, 20.2 <code>SPEC-PUB-CRASH-001</code>, and Appendix A.8 |\\n15951:| Approved v0.4.3 roadmap and macOS terminal-realm boundaries | Sections 2.2–2.3, 3.1–3.2, 4.2/4.4, 7.1, 12.1–12.3, 13.3/13.5–13.6/13.11/13.15, 14.1, 15.3, 16.2, 17.1, 19.1–19.4, and Appendix D |\\n15957:| Closed registry and embedded shapes | Sections 5.4–5.6, 7.5, 10.4, 18.1, and the exhaustive positive/negative fixture rules in Appendix D |\\n15969:| Contradictory environment overrides | One five-entry flag/environment registry, value-kind and empty/unknown rules in Section 3.2; identical precedence in Sections 6.1 and 14.2; <code>AC-PATH-001</code> and Appendix D fixtures |\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4006,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1002,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
