{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca2b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6e-3dc6-7091-89ac-ffb24ddb613d"},"sequence":880,"recorded_at":1780531400001755,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"33c437db-b2c4-4fed-b492-4dcd097e109a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad70-8c47-7a42-b569-17253def959f"},"task_id":"01a0ad70-8c47-7a42-b569-17253def959f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad70-8c47-7a42-b569-17253def959f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/provhost/profile.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|// This file maps execution profiles to provider adapter flags under\n4|// Section 7.7. The v0.3.0 yolo mappings below are exact adapter\n5|// strings the host persists into SpawnPlans; standard uses the\n6|// provider's normal approval and sandbox behavior and omits every\n7|// unrestricted flag. The adapter MUST probe the exact provider\n8|// version before applying a mapping, and an absent or changed flag\n9|// fails closed: unknown providers and unknown profiles are refused,\n10|// never defaulted.\n11|\n12|// Execution profiles Section 7.7 defines.\n13|const (\n14|\tProfileStandard = \"standard\"\n15|\tProfileYOLO     = \"yolo\"\n16|)\n17|\n18|// profileProviders lists the six Section 7.7 providers in table\n19|// order. Pi has no permission-mode flag: both of its profiles resolve\n20|// to the default full tool set, and probe and launch output MUST\n21|// disclose that equivalence rather than invent a flag.\n22|var profileProviders = []string{\n23|\t\"codex\",\n24|\t\"claude\",\n25|\t\"gemini\",\n26|\t\"muse\",\n27|\t\"antigravity\",\n28|\t\"pi\",\n29|}\n30|\n31|// profileYOLOMapping is the required yolo adapter flag per provider.\n32|// Standard maps to the empty string for every provider: no flag, no\n33|// alias that silently expands to unrestricted mode.\n34|var profileYOLOMapping = map[string]string{\n35|\t\"codex\":       \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n36|\t\"claude\":      \"--dangerously-skip-permissions\",\n37|\t\"gemini\":      \"--approval-mode=yolo\",\n38|\t\"muse\":        \"--yolo\",\n39|\t\"antigravity\": \"--dangerously-skip-permissions\",\n40|\t\"pi\":          \"default_unrestricted_tool_set\",\n41|}\n42|\n43|// profileNames is the exact Section 7.7 execution-profile vocabulary:\n44|// standard and yolo, nothing else. It is package-level so the closed\n45|// vocabulary census derives it: admitting a third profile here must\n46|// redden TestProfileNamesAreDerivedFromSpec, not resolve to a flag.\n47|var profileNames = map[string]bool{\n48|\tProfileStandard: true,\n49|\tProfileYOLO:     true,\n50|}\n51|\n52|// ProfileMapping resolves the adapter flag for one provider under one\n53|// profile. Standard returns the empty string: the caller omits every\n54|// unrestricted flag. An unknown provider or profile is an\n55|// invalid_config caller error; there is no default mapping a new\n56|// provider could silently inherit.\n57|func ProfileMapping(providerID, profile string) (string, error) {\n58|\tmapping, known := profileYOLOMapping[providerID]\n59|\tif !known {\n60|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"profile mapping names an unknown provider\")\n61|\t\tif err != nil {\n62|\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n63|\t\t}\n64|\t\treturn \"\", failure\n65|\t}\n66|\tif !profileNames[profile] {\n67|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"profile mapping names an unknown profile\")\n68|\t\tif err != nil {\n69|\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n70|\t\t}\n71|\t\treturn \"\", failure\n72|\t}\n73|\tif profile == ProfileYOLO {\n74|\t\treturn mapping, nil\n75|\t}\n76|\treturn \"\", nil\n77|}","final_result":true}}}
