d open extensions are bounded\\n32:// at 4 levels, so 256 leaves more than sixfold headroom over any accepted AX\\n33:// object. It is also far below encoding/json's 10,000-level Unmarshal cap and\\n34:// the unbounded recursion inside the JCS re-parse, so this typed refusal is\\n35:// always the first gate a deep document meets, and the decode stack stays at\\n36:// a few hundred small frames regardless of input size.\\n46:// SelfField is one of the pinned AX immutable-object self-identity namespaces.\\n47:// Chunk IDs are intentionally absent: Section 10.3 defines chunk_id as a\\n48:// digest of raw bytes, not of a JSON object.\\n===\\ninternal/canonicaljson/canonical.go:222:func Canonicalize(input []byte) ([]byte, error) {\\ninternal/canonicaljson/canonical.go:251:func CalculateObjectIdentity(input []byte) (scalar.Digest, SelfField, error) {\\ninternal/canonicaljson/canonical.go:309:func VerifyObjectIdentity(input []byte) (scalar.Digest, SelfField, error) {\\ninternal/canonicaljson/declared_byte_bounds.go:27:func CanonicalByteLength(value any) (int, error) {\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 1887,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 472,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
